"""FastAPI application.

Auth is a bearer token in `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (session token from
login, or a scoped, expiring API key). Every tenant route is scoped to the caller's
org_id — cross-tenant access returns 404 (existence is not leaked). `/health`,
`/auth/register`, `/auth/login`, `/auth/google`, `/auth/2fa/verify`, `/auth/verify`,
`/auth/verification/resend`, `/auth/forgot`, `/auth/reset`, and explicitly configured participant routes are public. Runs execute in-request
via BackgroundTasks — the arq worker replaces this in H0 hardening without
changing the routes.
"""

